{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>For he had broken loose.</b> Revealed and notorious for evil, in that his heart was exposed through this." "<b>That Aaron had let them break loose.</b> It revealed that there were no righteous men among them — for had righteous men been there to help Aaron when they gathered against him, Aaron would not have made the calf at all." "<b>For a derision among their enemies.</b> For an evil name among their enemies, who would say of them that they did not prove faithful to their covenant, that among them there is not even one who does good, and that they showed no respect for prophet or prince in their midst. And this is because even though not all of them — nor even the majority — gathered against Aaron, all of them were subject to derision for not having protested against those who rose up."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:47.495829380Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}